# Vision collage packing

Hard rule for diana’s dashboard (`/Users/diana/my-dashboard`) vision collage days.

This file lives here — `/Users/diana/my-dashboard/.cursor/rules/vision-collage-no-overlap.mdc`. When the packing rule changes, write it **here**. Do not leave the update only in task-dashboard.

## Goal name

Call it **vision collage**. Do **not** call it grid collage, equal 2×3, rooms, “air collage”, or “Sep 18 flat”.

## What VISION COLLAGE is (Sep 18+)

**Photo-shaped tiles packed as a mosaic** — asymmetric `visionPackSpec` (glow-up / fitness tall slots when those sections exist). Tiles **kiss** — **gap: 0**. No gutters / “air” between sections. Gold foil centered titles. **layout · carry · +** intact.

- Pack via `visionPackSpec(n, needSquare, hasTallBody, false)` — magazine / mosaic places, **not** the equal-cell `noBanner` branch
- **Never** 12px (or any) gutters on Sep 18+ — gaps were never authorized
- Fuller sections grow with content / tasks; empties stay at a base size
- Fill the board when there are **3+** sections — no empty strip, no leftover hole
- **Never overlap**
- Photos `cover` the tile (crop edges; no letterbox)
- Keep tile resize + photo reframe (glyph stays invisible)

## NEVER on Sep 18+ (hard bans)

- **Gaps / gutters / “air”** between tiles
- **Equal-cell 2×3 / flat grid** — that is **grid collage**, rejected
- Locking “equal 2×3” as if it were vision collage
- `packDashMosaic` / `tessellateDashRooms` / `dash-mosaic-era`
- “Balanced zigzag” / `airBalanced` that forces all landscape row-strips
- Stripping **layout**, day-count badges, resize, or reframe

